{"name":"Kaleidoscope","hex":"#8da8be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kaleidoscope","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instrument consisting of a tube containing mirrors and loose, colourful beads or other objects; when the tube is looked into and rotated, a succession of symmetrical designs can be seen. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A constantly changing series of colours or other things."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move in shifting (and often attractive or colourful) patterns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kaleidoscope"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kaleidoscope","blocks":[{"text":"A kaleidoscope is an optical instrument with two or more reflecting surfaces tilted to each other at an angle, so that one or more objects on one end of these mirrors are shown as a symmetrical pattern when viewed from the other end, due to repeated reflection. These reflectors are often enclosed in a tube, usually containing on one end a cell with loose, colored pieces of glass or other transparent materials to be reflected into the viewed pattern. Rotation of the cell causes motion of the materials, resulting in an ever-changing view being presented."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Kaleidoscope_tube_1.jpg/330px-Kaleidoscope_tube_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaleidoscope","wikidata":"Q180049"},{"title":"Kaleidoscope (American TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Kaleidoscope is an American heist drama television miniseries created by Eric Garcia. The eight-part series is an episodic anthology with standalone episodes. It centers on master thief Leo Pap and his crew attempting an epic heist worth $7 billion, but betrayal, greed and other threats undermine their plans. Kaleidoscope was released on January 1, 2023, by Netflix."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/2023_Kaleidoscope_%28TV_series%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaleidoscope_(American_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q108803630"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_39-40_%28kircher_-_bradley_comparison%29.jpg/500px-1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_39-40_%28kircher_-_bradley_comparison%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_39-40_%28kircher_-_bradley_comparison%29.jpg/500px-1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_39-40_%28kircher_-_bradley_comparison%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A comparison of the mirror constructions of Kircher (left) and Bradley (right)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_39-40_(kircher_-_bradley_comparison).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Kaleidoscopes.jpg/500px-Kaleidoscopes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Kaleidoscopes.jpg/1280px-Kaleidoscopes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Kaleidoscopes.jpg/500px-Kaleidoscopes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Patterns when seen through a kaleidoscope tube","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKaleidoscopes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_18-20.jpg/500px-1819_brewster_-_treatise_on_the_kaleidoscope_fig_18-20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_